      "line": 17,
      "purpose": "Which column of a sheet holds each row's id.",
      "note": "Spanish:  `- sus identificadores están en \"id\"`\nToday:  Runs:  the recipe box, on a real sheet.\nA (built, recommended):  `- its ids are in \"id\"`  --  short, the same shape as versions.\nB:  `- its ids are in the column \"id\"`  ·  `- sus identificadores están en la columna \"id\"`  --  says column, which is what a person sees, but only sheets have them, and the same shape on a server would be wrong.\nC:  `- a recipe's id is in \"id\"`  ·  `- el identificador de una receta está en \"id\"`  --  per type:  more words for the same line.\nWhy:  `identificadores` is long, and it's the glossary's word.\nRenaming it later:  4 lines in 4 files of rules, tests and docs, none in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
      "current": "- its ids are in \"id\"",
      "recommended": "- its ids are in \"id\""
    },
    {
      "id": "key-secret",
      "section": "details",
      "file": "parser/src/spell/rules/places/places.en.ts",
      "line": 18,
      "purpose": "Names a key the server side holds.  A key written into a program won't compile, since anyone can read it.",
      "note": "Spanish:  `- su clave es el secreto \"COOKBOOK_KEY\"`\nToday:  Compiles;  naming a key is tested, and using it waits for a kind of place that needs one (the Airtable phase).\nA (built, recommended):  `- its key is the secret \"COOKBOOK_KEY\"`  --  says it's a key, and that it isn't here.\nB:  `- its password is the secret \"COOKBOOK_KEY\"`  ·  `- su contraseña es el secreto \"COOKBOOK_KEY\"`  --  the everyday word, but a service's key isn't a password.\nC:  `- it signs in with the secret \"COOKBOOK_KEY\"`  ·  `- entra con el secreto \"COOKBOOK_KEY\"`  --  plain, but says something happens that doesn't, for a key sent on each request.\nWhy:  `clave` is both key and password in Spanish, so it reads well there.\nRenaming it later:  9 lines in 7 files of rules, tests and docs, none in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
      "current": "- its key is the secret \"COOKBOOK_KEY\"",
      "recommended": "- its key is the secret \"COOKBOOK_KEY\""
    },
    {
      "id": "checked-every",
      "section": "details",
      "file": "parser/src/spell/rules/places/places.en.ts",
      "line": 10,
      "purpose": "How often Spell asks a place what changed, for one that can't say so itself.  Without it, a web service warns.",
      "note": "Spanish:  `- se revisa cada 30 segundos`\nToday:  Runs:  the recipe box, on real servers.\nA (built, recommended):  `- it is checked every 30 seconds`  --  honest about what `live` means there, in the one place it needs saying, unlike the tools where `when` secretly means 15 minutes.\nB:  `- it is read again every 30 seconds`  ·  `- se lee de nuevo cada 30 segundos`  --  more exact, and longer.\nC:  `- refresh it every 30 seconds`  ·  `- recargar cada 30 segundos`  --  matches the `refresh` statement, but reads as an order, in a list of facts about the place.\nWhy:  Reads as a fact about the place, like its other lines.  Its warning in Spanish still names the kind in English:  `Un web service no puede ...`.\nRenaming it later:  18 lines in 9 files of rules, tests and docs, none in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
      "current": "- it is checked every 30 seconds",
      "recommended": "- it is checked every 30 seconds"
    },
    {
      "id": "saved-in",
