      "file": "parser/src/spell/rules/places/places.en.ts",
      "line": 26,
      "purpose": "ALREADY CHOSEN, reopenable.  That's all a type says:  from then on, a recipe you add or change is kept there, with no save step.",
      "note": "Spanish:  `- se guarda en el recetario familiar`\nToday:  Runs:  the recipe box, in English and Spanish.\nA (built, recommended):  `- it is saved in the family cookbook`  --  chosen by you (Q1).  Spell already says `is saved in its own file`, and Spanish had `se guarda en`.\nB:  `- it is kept in the family cookbook`  ·  `- se conserva en el recetario familiar`  --  the most natural English, with no hint of a step to do.  A second word for nearly one idea.\nC:  `- it comes from the family cookbook`  ·  `- viene del recetario familiar`  --  how Bubble and Retool say it, but nobody expects to write to where something comes from.\nD:  `- it lives in the family cookbook`  ·  `- vive en el recetario familiar`  --  your words at the kickoff.  `vive en` is odd in Spanish.\nWhy:  Decided.  What the parser found:  only a place's name may follow, or `is saved in its own file` reads `its own` as a property.\nRenaming it later:  86 lines in 33 files of rules, tests and docs, 9 lines in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
      "current": "- it is saved in the family cookbook",
      "recommended": "- it is saved in the family cookbook"
