      "line": 2251,
      "purpose": "All of them.  For a saved type, this now means all those in the place, not a scratch list of what the program made.",
      "note": "Spanish:  `cada receta`\nToday:  Runs:  the recipe box.  `the recipes` means the same, and is the plural form.\nA (built, recommended):  `every recipe`  --  the old word, reaching further.  One word tells one from many, as AppleScript's `every window` does.\nB:  `all recipes`  ·  `todas las recetas`  --  everyday too, and much the better Spanish:  `cada` means each, so `cada receta, ordenada` reads oddly next to `todas las recetas, ordenadas`.\nC:  `all the recipes`  ·  `todas las recetas`  --  the most spoken form, and one more word.\nWhy:  Keep the English, which every Spell program already reads.  Spanish could add `todas las recetas`, which doesn't compile today:  worth a look, as `cada` is why `ordenada` had to be singular.\nRenaming it later:  1232 lines in 423 files of rules, tests and docs, 282 lines in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
      "current": "every recipe",
      "recommended": "every recipe"
