      "purpose": "Only the ones that fit.  Compiled so the place does the filtering when it can.",
      "note": "Spanish:  `cada receta donde su título incluye la búsqueda`\nToday:  Runs:  the recipe box, in English and Spanish.  A condition the place can't answer, like this one, warns, and is worked out on the page.\nA (built, recommended):  `every recipe where its title includes the search`  --  Spell already used it (`the items in x where`), and it needs no verb first, unlike Bubble's `Do a search for`.\nB:  `every recipe whose title includes the search`  ·  `cada receta cuyo título incluye la búsqueda`  --  AppleScript's word, and elegant, but `whose` fits only a property, not `where it is quick`.\nC:  `every recipe that includes the search in its title`  ·  `cada receta que incluye la búsqueda en su título`  --  the most spoken form, and every condition would need its own wording.\nWhy:  One word that fits every condition.  `the recipes where ...`, which the first proposal also listed, doesn't compile:  only `every recipe where`.\nRenaming it later:  789 lines in 314 files of rules, tests and docs, 133 lines in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
      "current": "every recipe where its title includes the search",
