      "purpose": "In order of something about each one.  The place does it when it can.",
      "note": "Spanish:  `cada receta, ordenada por su título`\nToday:  Runs:  the recipe box, in English and Spanish.\nA (built, recommended):  `every recipe, sorted by its title`  --  what spreadsheets say (Sort).\nB:  `every recipe, ordered by its title`  ·  `cada receta, ordenada por su título`  --  SQL's word in English;  and the same as Spanish already.\nC:  `every recipe, in order of its title`  ·  `cada receta, en orden de su título`  --  reads aloud well, and needs no agreement in Spanish.  Longer.\nWhy:  Spanish takes four forms, and warns when one disagrees with its list.  The other way round (`from highest to lowest`) is proposed, and not built.\nRenaming it later:  21 lines in 11 files of rules, tests and docs, 2 lines in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
