      "line": 136,
      "purpose": "A sum.  Spell had no word for it.",
      "note": "Spanish:  `el total de sus precios`\nToday:  COMPILES TO THE WRONG THING:  in a real program it still reads a property called `total`, which isn't there, with no error.  The new rule loses to the older `the x of y`.\nA (built, recommended):  `the total of its prices`  --  a shopping receipt's word, the same in both languages.\nB:  `the sum of its prices`  ·  `la suma de sus precios`  --  Excel's word, and more mathematical.\nC:  `its prices added up`  ·  `sus precios sumados`  --  the plainest sentence, and it can't take `where` in front.\nWhy:  Keep the word, and fix the rule (a bug, not a word choice).  `the sum of its prices` falls into the same trap today, so it should get the same answer, or a hint.\nRenaming it later:  14 lines in 9 files of rules, tests and docs, 4 lines in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
