      "line": 316,
      "purpose": "The same thing, said a little more firmly.",
      "note": "Spanish:  `cada receta donde su cocinero es o bien \"Ana\" o \"Bo\"`\nToday:  Compiles to the right thing, in both languages.\nA (built, recommended):  `every recipe where its cook is either \"Ana\" or \"Bo\"`  --  Spell had `either` for declared values, and now it takes text too.\nB:  `every recipe where its cook is in [\"Ana\", \"Bo\"]`  ·  `cada receta donde su cocinero está en [\"Ana\", \"Bo\"]`  --  already works, and reads like a programmer.\nC:  drop it:  only is \"Ana\" or \"Bo\"  --  one way to say one thing, but people will type it anyway, and it would then be an error.\nWhy:  Costs nothing, and `o bien` is ordinary Spanish.\nRenaming it later:  30 lines in 16 files of rules, tests and docs, none in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
