      "purpose": "Words people bring from other tools.  They aren't Spell's, so a line starting with one says what to write instead.",
      "note": "Spanish:  `traer las recetas`\nToday:  Compiles to an error with a hint, on purpose.  Also `query`, `join`, `connect to`;  a program's own `to fetch the scores:` still wins.\nA (built, recommended):  `fetch the recipes`  --  keeps these words free, and teaches the real ones.\nB:  `get the recipes`  ·  `obtener las recetas`  --  already works today, with no new rule:  it declares a new `it`, so people from Shortcuts or HyperCard are fine.\nC:  fetch the recipes (a working synonym)  --  friendly, but then two ways to read, and no way back.\nWhy:  Also proposed, with no hint yet:  `database`, `relation`, `search for`.\nRenaming it later:  8 lines in 4 files of rules, tests and docs, none in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
