      "note": "Spanish:  `si no hay ninguna:`\nToday:  Runs:  the recipe box, in English and Spanish.\nA (built, recommended):  `if there are none:`  --  the sentence a person would say.\nB:  `if there aren't any:`  ·  `si no hay:`  --  more spoken.  `si no hay:` also spares Spanish the agreement, but it's clipped.\nC:  `if it is empty:`  ·  `si está vacía:`  --  a programmer's way to see it.  TRAP:  it compiles today, to a test of the program itself, not of the list.\nWhy:  `ninguna` agrees with what the loop reads, and warns if it doesn't.\nRenaming it later:  9 lines in 8 files of rules, tests and docs, 2 lines in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
