      "purpose": "Read everything again:  what a button under `if that fails:` does.",
      "note": "Spanish:  `reintentar`\nToday:  Runs:  the recipe box's Try again button.\nA (built, recommended):  `try again`  --  the button's own words.\nB:  `try again`  --  what the first proposal had for Spanish, and more everyday than `reintentar`, which reads as a software label.\nC:  `read again`  ·  `leer de nuevo`  --  more exact, and doesn't match the button anyone would draw.\nWhy:  Keep.  `reintentar` is also the common button label in Spanish apps, so it's the glossary's choice.\nRenaming it later:  12 lines in 10 files of rules, tests and docs, 3 lines in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
