      "purpose": "Adding it to the list is what keeps it.  `a new recipe` alone keeps nothing.  `remove` and `set` work the same.",
      "note": "Spanish:  `agregar (una nueva receta con título = el borrador) a las recetas`\nToday:  Runs:  the recipe box, on every back-end.\nA (built, recommended):  `add (a new recipe with title = the draft) to the recipes`  --  exactly what a program in memory writes today, and half-filled forms never reach the place.\nB:  `save (a new recipe with title = the draft)`  ·  `guardar (una nueva receta con título = el borrador)`  --  familiar, but then every program needs it, and forgetting it loses data silently.\nC:  `a new recipe with title = the draft`  ·  `una nueva receta con título = el borrador`  --  kept at once:  one step fewer, and half-filled forms land in the shared box.\nWhy:  HyperCard and Scratch's lesson:  no save command.\nRenaming it later:  9 lines in 3 files of rules, tests and docs, 6 lines in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
