      "purpose": "These steps go together:  if any fails, every one is put back.  Not every kind of place can truly promise it.",
      "note": "Spanish:  `todo o nada:`\nToday:  Runs, on a place in memory.\nA (built, recommended):  `all or nothing:`  --  an everyday phrase, the same in Spanish.\nB:  `together:`  ·  `juntos:`  --  short, but says nothing about failing, and agrees in gender.\nC:  `in one go:`  ·  `de una vez:`  --  reads well, and it's about speed in everyday speech.\nWhy:  Not offered:  `transaction`, a database word.\nRenaming it later:  16 lines in 12 files of rules, tests and docs, none in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
