      "section": "change",
      "file": "parser/src/spell/rules/places/places.en.ts",
      "line": 121,
      "purpose": "ALREADY CHOSEN, reopenable.  Forms are live by default, as you chose.  This is the rare exception:  a copy for an Edit screen with a Cancel button.",
      "note": "Spanish:  `un borrador de la receta`\nToday:  Compiles in both languages, on a thing a program has;  the engine under it is tested, and no test runs it from a Spell line.\nA (built, recommended):  `a draft of the recipe`  --  you chose live-by-default with this word (Q9).  COLLISION:  the Recipe Box has its own `draft`, a text, which is a different thing beside it.\nB:  `an edit of the recipe`  ·  `una edición de la receta`  --  no collision, and it matches `Edit screen`.  `save the edit` reads fine too.\nC:  `a working copy of the recipe`  ·  `una copia de trabajo de la receta`  --  exact, but `a copy of` already means a copy that forgets its original, and this one doesn't.\nWhy:  Keep:  `draft` says the right thing, and `save` refuses a plain text, saying why.  But it's the one word here that the flagship example uses for something else.\nRenaming it later:  14 lines in 11 files of rules, tests and docs, none in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
      "current": "a draft of the recipe",
      "recommended": "a draft of the recipe"
    },
    {
