      "file": "parser/src/spell/rules/places/places.en.ts",
      "line": 25,
      "purpose": "Keep the draft's changes.  The only `save` in the language.  Of anything else, it says there's no save step.",
      "note": "Spanish:  `guardar el borrador`\nToday:  Compiles of a real draft, and refused of anything else, in both languages;  no test saves one from a Spell line.\nA (built, recommended):  `save the draft`  --  what the button says.\nB:  `keep the draft`  ·  `conservar el borrador`  --  avoids the word `save` altogether, and reads as not throwing it away.\nC:  `apply the draft`  ·  `aplicar el borrador`  --  exact, and a settings-dialog word.\nWhy:  Goes with the row above, if that one changes.\nRenaming it later:  5 lines in 5 files of rules, tests and docs, none in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
      "current": "save the draft",
      "recommended": "save the draft"
    },
    {
