      "purpose": "Throw the draft's changes away.",
      "note": "Spanish:  `cancelar el borrador`\nToday:  Compiles of a real draft, in both languages;  no test runs it from a Spell line.\nA (built, recommended):  `cancel the draft`  --  what the Cancel button says.  `cancel` now has three uses:  an event, an action, a draft.\nB:  `throw away the draft`  ·  `descartar el borrador`  --  what the first proposal said, and it's the plainest.\nC:  `discard the draft`  ·  `descartar el borrador`  --  the same, as an app's dialog says it.\nWhy:  Keep:  a Cancel button is what it's for.\nRenaming it later:  3 lines in 3 files of rules, tests and docs, none in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
      "current": "cancel the draft",
