    {
      "id": "belongs",
      "section": "change",
      "file": "parser/src/spell/rules/classes/classes.en.ts",
      "line": 529,
      "purpose": "ALREADY CHOSEN, reopenable.  Removing the recipe removes its ingredients too, and undo brings them back.  Things in memory behave as before.",
      "note": "Spanish:  `un ingrediente pertenece a una receta`\nToday:  Runs, on a place in memory, for saved types.\nA (built, recommended):  `an ingredient belongs to one recipe`  --  you chose this meaning (Q10).  The words were there, and read as people expect.\nB:  `an ingredient is part of one recipe`  ·  `un ingrediente es parte de una receta`  --  says the same, with no new meaning for old words, and one more phrase.\nC:  `a recipe owns its ingredients`  ·  `una receta posee sus ingredientes`  --  from the other side, and `owns` and `posee` sound legal.\nWhy:  Decided.  In a saved owner, it's kept inside that owner's row, so it can't be asked for by itself.\nRenaming it later:  112 lines in 50 files of rules, tests and docs, 9 lines in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
