      "note": "Spanish:  `recargar las recetas`\nToday:  Compiles;  the engine under it is tested, and no test runs it from a Spell line.\nA (built, recommended):  `refresh the recipes`  --  every browser's button.  `actualizar`, the usual Spanish, already means a version upgrade in Spell.\nB:  `reload the recipes`  ·  `recargar las recetas`  --  the same button, and it would line up with the Spanish.  `load` stays free as a word people name their own actions with.\nC:  `read the recipes again`  ·  `leer de nuevo las recetas`  --  exact, and the longest.\nWhy:  Keep:  close, and `refresh` is what people call it.\nRenaming it later:  7 lines in 6 files of rules, tests and docs, 1 line in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
