      "note": "Spanish:  `- para publicar (una receta):  - está en \"/recetas/publicar\"`\nToday:  NEITHER COMPILES on the real parser today.  B fails on its address.  A is what's built, and the action reads, but its detail line `- it is at \"...\"` is refused in all 6 forms I tried, English and Spanish;  only the prototype's test parser reads it.  Written here on one line:  in a program, A's detail is indented under the action.\nA (built, recommended):  `- to publish (a recipe):  - it is at \"/recipes/publish\"`  --  two lines per operation, and no change to how an action is read;  it can take the details any action takes, as `- undone as` does.\nB:  `- to publish (a recipe) is at \"/recipes/publish\"`  ·  `- para publicar (una receta) está en \"/recetas/publicar\"`  --  one line, but `to ...` would have to learn to stop at `is at`, so a program's action with those words in its name changes meaning.\nWhy:  A, as built.  Picking B changes only that one rule and its Spanish.  Either way the rule needs fixing:  no test covers it on the real parser.\nRenaming it later:  2 lines in 2 files of rules, tests and docs, none in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
