      "note": "Spanish:  `la persona actual`\nToday:  Still being built:  it compiles on this branch's unfinished work, and runs in its tests.  Not committed.\nA (built, recommended):  `the current person`  --  plain.  Bubble's `Current user` shows people cope, and WWOD says people, not users.\nB:  `you`  ·  `tú`  --  the shortest, but who's `you`, to someone writing a program?  And Spanish splits into `tú` and `usted`.\nC:  `me`  ·  `yo`  --  short, and the person writing it isn't the one using it.\nWhy:  A program's own `current person` wins.\nRenaming it later:  10 lines in 7 files of rules, tests and docs, 1 line in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
