      "note": "Spanish:  `las personas presentes`\nToday:  Still being built:  it compiles on this branch's unfinished work, and warns on a place that can only ever see you.\nA (built, recommended):  `the people here`  --  reads as a room does, which matches `live room`.\nB:  `everyone here`  ·  `todos aquí`  --  more spoken, and Spanish's word leaves out half of them unless written with care.\nC:  `the people in the room`  ·  `las personas en la sala`  --  nice on a live room, and wrong on any other kind of place.\nWhy:  A program's own `people here` wins.  `the people editing it`, `when someone arrives:` and `when someone leaves:` were proposed too, and aren't being built.\nRenaming it later:  13 lines in 10 files of rules, tests and docs, 1 line in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
