      "note": "Spanish:  `Usar datos de ejemplo`\nToday:  The engine runs, and is tested.  The switch people will see is epic `editor`'s, not built, so these words are only proposals.\nA (built, recommended):  `Use a sample`  --  short, and `sample data` is a common phrase.\nB:  `Try with made-up data`  ·  `Probar con datos inventados`  --  plainest, but its first records may be copied from the real place, so it isn't always made up.\nC:  `Use a practice copy`  ·  `Usar una copia de práctica`  --  says it's safe to change, and is a word no other tool uses.\nWhy:  Avoid `muestra` in Spanish:  it's a specimen.  No language word follows from this, so it's the cheapest row here.\nRenaming it later:  17 lines in 6 files of rules, tests and docs, none in the built-in projects, none in your own projects.",
